  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "nJBBWLMo5NnYwhHK8P8CRz/Jvc8=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:18:06.261Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The reactor's unit of storage is not the document \u2014 it is the `(documentId, scope, branch)` triple. Each triple maintains its own operation sequence, which is what lets a private draft in `local` and published content in `global` advance independently on the same document.\n\nThe operation itself is deliberately narrow:\n\n```ts\ntype Operation = {\n  id: string;              // stable derived operation id\n  index: number;           // sequential index WITHIN the scope\n  skip: number;            // skip count for reshuffle/undo\n  timestampUtcMs: string;\n  hash: string;            // content hash for verification\n  error?: string;          // message from a failed action\n  resultingState?: string; // serialized state after applying\n  action: Action;\n};\n```\n\nNote what is absent: **scope and branch are not fields on the operation.** They are carried in `OperationContext` alongside it. So `index` only means anything relative to a scope, and an operation moved between contexts would be meaningless \u2014 which is why the reactor always passes operations as `OperationWithContext`.\n\nFour scopes are recognised by convention: `global` (shared state), `local` (per-user state such as preferences), `document` (system operations \u2014 `CREATE_DOCUMENT`, `DELETE_DOCUMENT`, `UPGRADE_DOCUMENT`, relationships), and any custom scope an application defines.\n\n## Provenance\n- `packages/reactor/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` \u2014 Core Concepts \u203a Operation and Scope\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:18:06.260Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:18:06.261Z"
    }
  },
